From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:57:44 +0200
Subject: clk: sunxi-ng: a64: Allow PLL-MIPI down to 432 MHz

The PinePhone's XBD599 mode has a 72 MHz pixel clock, which over 4 DSI
lanes at 24 bpp needs TCON0 at 432 MHz. With PLL-MIPI's floor at the
user manual's 500 MHz the panel refreshes at 69.4 Hz instead of 60.

fboot runs PLL-MIPI at 432 MHz (PLL-VIDEO0 297 MHz, n 8 k 2 m 11) and
the panel measures 60.006 Hz there. The n/m ratio and parent/m
constraints still hold at that rate.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun50i-a64.c
@@ -208,7 +208,12 @@ static struct ccu_nkm pll_mipi_clk = {
 					      &ccu_nkm_ops,
 					      CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE | CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT),
 		.features	= CCU_FEATURE_CLOSEST_RATE,
-		.min_rate	= 500000000,
+		/*
+		 * The user manual says 500 MHz, but the PinePhone's XBD599
+		 * mode (72 MHz, 4 lanes, 24 bpp) needs 432 MHz on TCON0 for
+		 * 60 Hz. The n/m and parent/m constraints above still hold.
+		 */
+		.min_rate	= 432000000,
 		.max_rate	= 1400000000,
 	},
 };
